  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I am my beloved’s, and my beloved is mine: he feedeth among the lilies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Thou art beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as an army with banners.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair is as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Thy teeth are as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, whereof every one beareth twins, and there is not one barren among them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "As a piece of a pomegranate are thy temples within thy locks.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "My dove, my undefiled is but one; she is the only one of her mother, she is the choice one of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; yea, the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Who is she that looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, and terrible as an army with banners?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, and to see whether the vine flourished, and the pomegranates budded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Or ever I was aware, my soul made me like the chariots of Amminadib.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Song of Solomon 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:song-of-solomon:6:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
